Looking at the jagged edges: pieces A and B have matching single‑bump top edges, C and D have matching double‑bump top edges, A and D have matching double‑notch right edges, and B and C have matching single‑notch right edges. These four pieces (A, B, C, D) can pair up all eight jagged edges perfectly to form the interior cuts of the square.

Piece E, however, has a top edge (one large bump followed by a long dip and flick) that matches no other piece's edge, so it cannot be fitted into the square.

\boxed{E}
